1
00:00:02,433 --> 00:00:08,800
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]
- Siklab! Siklab! Siklab!

2
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:17,967
[CHEERING CONTINUES]

3
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:28,067
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]
- Siklab! Siklab! Siklab!

4
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:40,633
[CHEERING CONTINUES]

5
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:47,833
Siklab-ers!

6
00:00:47,967 --> 00:00:50,567
Are you ready?

7
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:55,100
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

8
00:00:55,233 --> 00:00:57,200
Because of all of you,
this is now...

9
00:00:57,333 --> 00:01:00,467
the number one song
in the Philippines!

10
00:01:01,467 --> 00:01:03,867
Thank you so much. Let's go!

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,500
[SIKLAB PERFORMING
"THIS IS MY VOICE"]

12
00:01:07,667 --> 00:01:17,633
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,833
Stayed quiet in the corner
of the room.

14
00:01:21,967 --> 00:01:26,367
Listening as everyone else
broke through.

15
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:30,600
Every voice was loud
and clear.

16
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:36,033
While I kept my words beneath
the sound.

17
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:39,533
Tried so hard to follow
every wave.

18
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:44,067
Singing lines that never
felt like mine.

19
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:48,367
Until my heart got tired
of pretending.

20
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:53,533
Like I was someone else again.

21
00:01:53,667 --> 00:02:00,400
This is my voice,
shaking but it's honest.

22
00:02:00,533 --> 00:02:05,700
It's honest,
I don't need to change it,

23
00:02:05,833 --> 00:02:08,033
just to make them want it.

24
00:02:08,167 --> 00:02:11,933
And even if I fall...

25
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:19,200
this is my voice.

26
00:02:19,367 --> 00:02:21,233
Siklab! Siklab!

27
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:32,033
[AUDIENCE SHOUTING]

28
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:37,533
This is my voice.

29
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:40,967
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

30
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:50,667
This is my voice.

31
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:59,600
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

32
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:04,667
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]
- Siklab! Siklab!

33
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:12,167
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

34
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,467
Miguel! Miguel!

35
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,333
Miguel!

36
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:19,800
[SHOUTING CONTINUES]

37
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:22,767
Bye.

38
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:24,767
Bye. Bye, guys!

39
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,600
- Miguel!
- Bye, everyone.

40
00:03:26,733 --> 00:03:36,367
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

41
00:03:49,267 --> 00:03:50,900
Are you sure about this, Miguel?

42
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:52,967
You're going to busk in public?

43
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:54,500
What if someone recognizes you?

44
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,233
Don't worry, Bro.

45
00:03:57,367 --> 00:03:58,867
No one will recognize me.

46
00:03:59,567 --> 00:04:02,133
I'll just modulate my voice
so no one will recognize me.

47
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:05,867
I just want to sing again
without being mobbed.

48
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,367
If you get caught,
you're in trouble.

49
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,800
Seriously, Miguel.

50
00:04:11,933 --> 00:04:15,267
And your dad is definitely
going to be furious.

51
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:19,867
Whatever.

52
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:41,167
[UPBEAT MUSIC]

53
00:04:55,333 --> 00:05:03,233
[SOFT MUSIC]

54
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,733
Oh no, the curry spilled
in my bag!

55
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,533
And this is my favorite bag!

56
00:05:19,033 --> 00:05:20,367
Sorry, I'm sorry.

57
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,767
Hey, get back here!

58
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,033
Hey, teddy bear!

59
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:29,533
Never knew a name could be.

60
00:05:32,333 --> 00:05:38,367
A melody that follows me.

61
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:45,000
[MIGUEL SINGING
"IKAW LANG (WHAT I CAN'T SAY)"]

62
00:05:45,133 --> 00:05:51,767
Feelings inside my chest...

63
00:05:54,333 --> 00:06:01,300
rising up to my throat.

64
00:06:02,667 --> 00:06:08,367
If I say it out loud,
will you even listen?

65
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:11,800
Finally, I caught you,
you troublemaking teddy bear.

66
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:17,067
You're the one who spilled
chicken curry on my bag.

67
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:21,567
For your information,

68
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:25,933
curcumin in curry can chemically
bind to fabric fibers.

69
00:06:26,067 --> 00:06:27,933
Look, the stain won't come out.

70
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,767
Miss!

71
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,033
What was that?

72
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:38,933
The song was already beautiful,
and then you had to ruin it.

73
00:06:45,367 --> 00:06:46,767
Miss, I'm really sorry.

74
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,133
Let's talk later.

75
00:06:48,267 --> 00:06:50,633
I promise, after my set.

76
00:06:50,767 --> 00:06:51,767
I'm sorry.

77
00:06:52,933 --> 00:07:02,767
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:31,667
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,633
I'm sorry I ran off
when I stained your bag.

80
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:57,400
Here.

81
00:07:57,533 --> 00:07:58,800
I got you a new one.

82
00:07:58,933 --> 00:08:01,067
It's the same brand, but they
didn't have it in white anymore.

83
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:03,900
So, I hope you like blue.

84
00:08:05,167 --> 00:08:06,900
Go on, take it.

85
00:08:07,033 --> 00:08:09,633
Come on, so teddy bear won't be
sad anymore.

86
00:08:11,633 --> 00:08:12,767
Here, take it.

87
00:08:14,467 --> 00:08:15,567
Please.

88
00:08:16,533 --> 00:08:17,633
Don't be mad anymore.

89
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,800
Wait.

90
00:08:29,933 --> 00:08:32,067
How did you buy this
when you were busking earlier?

91
00:08:33,167 --> 00:08:34,533
I had my PA buy it.

92
00:08:37,733 --> 00:08:39,433
I mean, I asked a friend
to get it.

93
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:41,667
[GENTLE MUSIC]

94
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,933
Please don't be mad
at me anymore.

95
00:08:44,067 --> 00:08:44,933
I'm really sorry.

96
00:08:47,567 --> 00:08:48,733
Friends?

97
00:08:50,867 --> 00:08:52,067
Fine.

98
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,200
Friends.

99
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:02,033
Go on, open it.

100
00:09:13,633 --> 00:09:14,767
Do you approve?

101
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,167
Thank you.

102
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:39,167
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:10:15,733 --> 00:10:17,700
Every Friday...

104
00:10:17,833 --> 00:10:19,633
he sings at Manila Park.

105
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:36,033
He never told me
who he really was.

106
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,867
He said it was a secret.

107
00:10:59,133 --> 00:11:01,733
All I know is that
we're the same age.

108
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:07,867
If only...

109
00:11:08,033 --> 00:11:10,100
So, I gave him a nickname.

110
00:11:13,933 --> 00:11:15,867
"Captain Serenade,"

111
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,933
because he always wears
that captain-style cap.

112
00:11:18,067 --> 00:11:20,667
the things...

113
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:26,400
you helped me get through.

114
00:11:26,533 --> 00:11:28,733
And he sings so beautifully.

115
00:11:31,933 --> 00:11:35,767
Wanted to stop dreaming.

116
00:11:36,967 --> 00:11:45,833
You gave me something I want
to hold on to.

117
00:11:47,933 --> 00:11:50,467
I'd tell you I'm sorry.

118
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:54,667
Bet you thought you knew me well

119
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,933
I hope you felt the two words.

120
00:12:02,067 --> 00:12:08,733
I couldn't say to you...

121
00:12:09,633 --> 00:12:12,167
I love you.

122
00:12:17,333 --> 00:12:19,733
But one day...

123
00:12:19,867 --> 00:12:21,900
we suddenly stopped seeing each
other.

124
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:31,667
[POIGNANT MUSIC]

125
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,167
This next song is also
an original

126
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:38,367
and I wrote it for someone
who isn't here.

127
00:12:40,667 --> 00:12:47,433
Feelings inside my chest...

128
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:56,100
rising up to my throat.

129
00:12:57,300 --> 00:13:00,133
If I say it out loud.

130
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:04,767
Will you listen to me?

131
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:11,400
Or should I just keep my mouth
shut?

132
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:25,400
My crooked smile trembles
with nerves.

133
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:34,167
My lips are dry,
aching with longing.

134
00:13:35,367 --> 00:13:43,367
I can't say it.

135
00:13:44,467 --> 00:13:52,533
I just can't say it

136
00:13:55,400 --> 00:14:02,733
Cause baby,
you are my favorite song.

137
00:14:02,867 --> 00:14:06,067
I'll put you on repeat
all night.

138
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:10,067
I know I'll never move on.

139
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:13,533
My first, right where I belong.

140
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:20,867
You are my first heartbeat song.

141
00:14:21,767 --> 00:14:25,933
[MELLOW MUSIC]

142
00:14:26,067 --> 00:14:28,800
I never made it back
to Manila Park.

143
00:14:30,167 --> 00:14:33,133
Based on the results,
Sir has pancreatic cancer.

144
00:14:33,833 --> 00:14:38,033
My grandfather was diagnosed
with stage 3 pancreatic cancer.

145
00:14:39,433 --> 00:14:43,300
The doctor said he only had
about a year left to live.

146
00:14:43,967 --> 00:14:47,500
But Grandfather Xavi refused
chemotherapy...

147
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:51,500
no matter how much we begged
him.

148
00:14:59,167 --> 00:15:01,167
I'm not going through treatment
anymore.

149
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:03,667
It's just a waste of money.

150
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:06,467
- Dad.
- Grandfather, please.

151
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:09,367
We can ask politicians for help.

152
00:15:09,833 --> 00:15:12,333
What?

153
00:15:12,467 --> 00:15:16,133
They're the ones stealing
from us.

154
00:15:16,267 --> 00:15:19,133
And you'd trade my dignity
just to get their help?

155
00:15:19,267 --> 00:15:20,200
No.

156
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:24,567
You know...

157
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,333
all I really want is this...

158
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:29,500
I don't want you to struggle
or be more stressed.

159
00:15:30,933 --> 00:15:32,500
Okay?

160
00:15:32,633 --> 00:15:34,733
Most of all...

161
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:37,133
I don't want to leave you
with nothing.

162
00:15:39,133 --> 00:15:40,900
I hope you understand that.

163
00:15:46,133 --> 00:15:47,567
I'm already old.

164
00:15:50,133 --> 00:15:52,433
I'm ready to meet the Lord.

165
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,767
Do you think everything you
cooked today will be finished?

166
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:12,767
Mama Bebe, Grandfather Xavi.

167
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,867
What?

168
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,633
- Surprise!
- Wow!

169
00:16:17,767 --> 00:16:19,533
So even though it hurt,

170
00:16:19,667 --> 00:16:22,633
Grandfather Xavi and I went
ahead with his bucket list.

171
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:26,633
Are you ready for
"Grandpa Xavi's Bucket List"?

172
00:16:26,767 --> 00:16:30,300
It's a list of things he wants
to do before he's gone.

173
00:16:33,267 --> 00:16:35,700
"Put a medal on A..."

174
00:16:35,833 --> 00:16:37,200
Of course.

175
00:16:37,333 --> 00:16:39,267
That's what we've always been
hoping for, right?

176
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,500
Of course.

177
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:41,567
You promise, right?

178
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:44,567
- That's a promise.
- We'll make that happen.

179
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:45,633
Ah, okay.

180
00:16:45,767 --> 00:16:46,800
Are you ready for the next one?

181
00:16:46,933 --> 00:16:48,533
So, what's next?

182
00:16:48,667 --> 00:16:49,733
Next.

183
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:52,733
"Go to..."

184
00:16:52,867 --> 00:16:55,100
- Dad, really.
- Me?

185
00:16:55,233 --> 00:16:56,900
Really? With...

186
00:16:57,033 --> 00:16:58,533
How did you know?

187
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:01,333
- Of course I know that.
- Dad is clearly very excited.

188
00:17:01,467 --> 00:17:02,700
- Very excited.
- I think I'd like that.

189
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:05,533
- Okay. Next.
- All right.

190
00:17:05,667 --> 00:17:07,333
Let's go to number four first.

191
00:17:07,467 --> 00:17:08,833
Number four...

192
00:17:08,967 --> 00:17:11,267
Hey, I like that too...

193
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,333
- to travel...
- To go swimming.

194
00:17:12,467 --> 00:17:15,100
I've always wanted to see
resorts like that.

195
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:16,533
- Yes, the white sand beaches.
- I could learn a lot from that.

196
00:17:16,667 --> 00:17:18,533
Dad, they say it's really
beautiful.

197
00:17:18,667 --> 00:17:20,967
- Yes, we'll go there.
- I'm so excited.

198
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,133
- White sand.
- Yes.

199
00:17:22,267 --> 00:17:24,000
- Yes.
- The white sands of Boracay.

200
00:17:24,967 --> 00:17:26,633
Number five...

201
00:17:26,767 --> 00:17:28,700
"Find a partner for..."

202
00:17:28,833 --> 00:17:30,767
Dad, you really went there.

203
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,300
You even dragged me into this.

204
00:17:32,433 --> 00:17:34,267
- Unbelievable.
- He's just reading my mind.

205
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,200
- Oh my.
- I'm not saying anything...

206
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:37,600
but if there's a chance...

207
00:17:37,733 --> 00:17:40,833
All right, if there's a chance.

208
00:17:40,967 --> 00:17:42,867
That's your challenge.

209
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,633
Let's see about that, Mama Bebe.

210
00:17:44,767 --> 00:17:45,833
Oh, what could this be?

211
00:17:45,967 --> 00:17:47,100
- Okay, what's number one?
- This is the grand finale.

212
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:50,000
Number one,
this is the most important.

213
00:17:51,533 --> 00:17:53,167
"To build..."

214
00:17:53,967 --> 00:17:55,300
Yes.

215
00:17:55,433 --> 00:17:58,067
And number one on Grandfather
Xavi's list...

216
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:01,100
is to build and make successful
the dream resort

217
00:18:01,233 --> 00:18:02,300
he and Grandmother Marie always
wanted,

218
00:18:02,433 --> 00:18:04,500
before they meet again
in heaven.

219
00:18:07,967 --> 00:18:09,967
I hope we can make all of that
come true.

220
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:11,700
We'll make it happen, Dad.

221
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,167
Thank you, my grandchild.

222
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:18,700
Oh my.

223
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:20,900
If we manage to do all that...

224
00:18:21,033 --> 00:18:22,533
your grandmother will be
so happy.

225
00:18:25,233 --> 00:18:28,333
Come on, have some turon
for snacks.

226
00:18:28,467 --> 00:18:31,767
- Thank you, Mama Bebe.
- It's ready.

227
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:33,000
You know...

228
00:18:33,133 --> 00:18:35,133
we were so happy that day.

229
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,800
Have it with some leche flan.

230
00:18:38,933 --> 00:18:40,867
While we were laughing,

231
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,767
even just for a moment...

232
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:46,700
we forgot all our problems.

233
00:18:46,833 --> 00:18:48,067
Is it good, Dad?

234
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,400
Where's the jackfruit?

235
00:18:50,533 --> 00:18:52,733
I mixed in leche flan instead.

236
00:18:52,867 --> 00:18:55,500
It has leche flan inside.

237
00:18:55,667 --> 00:18:57,000
That's my specialty.

238
00:18:57,133 --> 00:18:58,133
No wonder it's all gone.

239
00:18:58,267 --> 00:19:01,100
Yes, but if you want more,
you can have some.

240
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:11,467
<i> You're probably wondering,</i>

241
00:19:12,167 --> 00:19:14,833
<i>how someone like me
could build a resort.</i>

242
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:20,967
<i>Good thing I'm not like other
16-year-olds,</i>

243
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:24,700
<i> because my IQ is 156.</i>

244
00:19:25,367 --> 00:19:27,767
<i>That's considered genius level,
according to studies.</i>

245
00:19:29,867 --> 00:19:32,267
<i>And to make Grandfather Xavi's
dream come true...</i>

246
00:19:33,633 --> 00:19:36,900
<i>I studied everything
about building a resort.</i>

247
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:46,967
Mm.

248
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:49,267
- Have some milk tea first.
- Thank you, Grandfather.

249
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:54,667
<i>But I realized intelligence
alone isn't enough...</i>

250
00:19:55,933 --> 00:19:57,800
<i> because we're not rich.</i>

251
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:00,800
I'm getting sleepy.

252
00:20:00,933 --> 00:20:01,900
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

253
00:20:02,067 --> 00:20:03,200
Don't stay up too late.

254
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:05,200
- Yes.
- Get some rest.

255
00:20:05,333 --> 00:20:06,400
Thank you, Grandfather.

256
00:20:13,633 --> 00:20:15,400
- Good night.
- Good night.

257
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:23,167
<i>I had to be resourceful
to build our dream resort.</i>

258
00:20:27,767 --> 00:20:37,700
["YOU ARE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

259
00:20:45,333 --> 00:20:47,867
<i>We sold everything
we had in Manila...</i>

260
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:50,500
<i> so we could move to...</i>

261
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:52,333
<i> Solmera City.</i>

262
00:20:52,467 --> 00:20:54,867
<i>It's three hours away
from Manila</i>

263
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,467
<i> and it's similar to Cebu City.</i>

264
00:20:59,233 --> 00:21:01,967
It's modern,
but it has beautiful beaches.

265
00:21:02,867 --> 00:21:09,033
<i> You are my favorite song</i>

266
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:12,833
<i> You're my first hello to love</i>

267
00:21:12,967 --> 00:21:16,433
<i>My first, right where I belong.</i>

268
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:21,500
<i>That's where the beach property
Grandmother left us is located.</i>

269
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:29,000
<i>It was pawned when she got sick
and passed away.</i>

270
00:21:30,767 --> 00:21:32,833
<i>But Grandfather Xavi
was able to reclaim it</i>

271
00:21:32,967 --> 00:21:35,600
<i>using his retirement pay
from the government.</i>

272
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,633
[WAVES LAPPING]

273
00:21:52,767 --> 00:21:54,467
- Come on, my grandchild.
- Okay.

274
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,400
- Look at that.
- [ANGEL CHUCKLES]

275
00:21:57,533 --> 00:21:58,833
- See? Isn't it beautiful?
- Come on, Grandfather Xavi.

276
00:21:58,967 --> 00:22:00,367
Look at that.

277
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:01,733
- Hurry up.
- It's so beautiful.

278
00:22:01,867 --> 00:22:04,467
You know, a sunset
only lasts a moment.

279
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:05,967
- [ANGEL AND BEBE LAUGH]
- It doesn't last long,

280
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:07,533
but it's incredibly beautiful.

281
00:22:07,667 --> 00:22:09,100
- Oh, Dad.
- All right.

282
00:22:09,233 --> 00:22:11,100
- Easy now.
- Aww.

283
00:22:11,233 --> 00:22:12,900
Look, look.

284
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:14,533
That's all ours.

285
00:22:15,833 --> 00:22:16,800
[BEBE EXHALES]

286
00:22:18,633 --> 00:22:21,400
When your grandmother
and I got this property...

287
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:24,767
we never let it go.

288
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:28,367
So many people tried
to buy it from us,

289
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:31,700
but we never accepted
any of their offers.

290
00:22:31,833 --> 00:22:36,100
Even when we made a mistake
and pawned it,

291
00:22:36,533 --> 00:22:38,367
as soon as I received
my retirement pay,

292
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,300
I redeemed it right away.

293
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:43,467
This is where you'll see
the most beautiful sunset

294
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:45,367
in all of Solmera City.

295
00:22:46,833 --> 00:22:48,133
[CHUCKLES]

296
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,333
After all the years
we've held onto this,

297
00:22:50,467 --> 00:22:52,567
so many people have tried
to buy it.

298
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:57,333
- But, Dad, do you think...
-[ANGEL EXHALES]

299
00:22:57,467 --> 00:22:59,833
your remaining retirement money
will be enough

300
00:22:59,967 --> 00:23:01,967
and what little I've saved
from selling turon

301
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:04,367
to build our resort?

302
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:07,233
The resorts we passed
by were all so beautiful,

303
00:23:07,367 --> 00:23:09,167
especially that Monta...

304
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:11,300
Montaverde Group of Hotels.

305
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:13,167
It has such a nice name, right?

306
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:15,100
The owner must be a billionaire.

307
00:23:15,233 --> 00:23:16,267
- Maybe.
- Oh my.

308
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:18,800
But we don't have to compete
with them, right?

309
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:22,033
- Mm-hmm.
- We can do this, Mom Bebe.

310
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:23,733
I've already calculated

311
00:23:23,867 --> 00:23:24,867
Grandfather Xavi's remaining
money.

312
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,267
So if we start with three
starter villas,

313
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:29,467
at 180,000 pesos each,

314
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:32,400
using light materials
and basic finishes,

315
00:23:32,533 --> 00:23:36,300
then 150,000 pesos will go
to permits and utilities.

316
00:23:36,433 --> 00:23:38,933
And the remaining 205,000 pesos

317
00:23:39,067 --> 00:23:42,700
will cover initial operations
and staff salaries.

318
00:23:42,833 --> 00:23:46,200
So if our monthly expenses
are 60,000 pesos

319
00:23:46,333 --> 00:23:49,300
and we charge 3,500 pesos
per night

320
00:23:49,433 --> 00:23:51,400
with a 50 percent
occupancy rate,

321
00:23:51,533 --> 00:23:54,567
that gives us a monthly gross
of 150,000 pesos,

322
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:57,667
we'll break even in about seven
to eight months.

323
00:23:57,833 --> 00:24:03,500
So it's possible we'll see
a full return within the year.

324
00:24:03,633 --> 00:24:07,767
There's also a big chance
we could lose money,

325
00:24:07,900 --> 00:24:10,967
but as long as occupancy
doesn't drop below 20 percent,

326
00:24:11,100 --> 00:24:12,200
we'll manage.

327
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:14,367
[XAVI AND ANGEL LAUGH]

328
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:16,500
- [BEBE EXHALES SHARPLY]
- [LAUGHTER]

329
00:24:17,433 --> 00:24:19,467
- [LAUGHS]
- So, Dad?

330
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,900
Ah, where did all that
come from?

331
00:24:22,033 --> 00:24:23,933
I didn't understand
what you said,

332
00:24:24,067 --> 00:24:25,267
- my dear, but...
- Oh, Grandfather Xavi.

333
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:27,767
But the way you said it...

334
00:24:28,767 --> 00:24:30,400
it sounded convincing.

335
00:24:30,533 --> 00:24:32,733
You're right, my dear.
We can do this.

336
00:24:32,867 --> 00:24:34,433
- [ANGEL LAUGHS]
- What?

337
00:24:34,567 --> 00:24:37,133
Me, I'll just say this...

338
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:39,467
- group hug!
- Group hug!

339
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:41,567
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

340
00:24:43,833 --> 00:24:46,700
<i>The next three months
weren't easy.</i>

341
00:24:46,833 --> 00:24:50,033
<i>We did everything
to finish the resort.</i>

342
00:24:50,733 --> 00:24:55,100
<i>We poured all the money
we had into it.</i>

343
00:24:55,233 --> 00:24:58,967
<i> You are my favorite song</i>

344
00:25:12,533 --> 00:25:14,667
- [ZION GROANS]
- I'm not beating you up.

345
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,867
I just need a scratch paper.

346
00:25:18,833 --> 00:25:19,667
- Is that an equation?
- Thank you

347
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:22,733
for being a sacrifice.

348
00:25:24,467 --> 00:25:26,333
There, write on that.
Go on.

349
00:25:26,467 --> 00:25:27,967
- [DASH CHUCKLES]
- [ZION GROANS]

350
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,800
Calix, please.

351
00:25:29,933 --> 00:25:31,867
The bell's about to ring,
ma'am is coming.

352
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,733
- Scratch paper.
- Yo, Calix.

353
00:25:33,867 --> 00:25:36,300
What if we write on his glasses
instead?

354
00:25:36,467 --> 00:25:38,033
- Yeah, Bro.
- Excuse me.

355
00:25:38,167 --> 00:25:39,433
- Let me see.
- Excuse me!

356
00:25:39,567 --> 00:25:40,800
Hey, what are you doing to him?

357
00:25:40,933 --> 00:25:42,167
Stop it.

358
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:45,567
- [CHUCKLING]
- Who is this?

359
00:25:48,233 --> 00:25:49,667
And who the hell are you?

360
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:51,867
[SOFT TENSE MUSIC]

361
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:54,233
[LAUGHTER]

362
00:25:54,367 --> 00:25:56,000
Oh, wait.

363
00:25:56,933 --> 00:25:57,867
Let me guess.

364
00:25:58,833 --> 00:26:00,633
You're the new junior high
transferee.

365
00:26:00,767 --> 00:26:03,067
- Ahh. That's her.
- Right?

366
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,300
Oh.

367
00:26:04,567 --> 00:26:06,433
Yes, that's me.

368
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,600
It's 2026, and bullying
is still the best

369
00:26:09,767 --> 00:26:11,533
your brain cells can do?

370
00:26:14,633 --> 00:26:17,467
You hurt others
just to look tough.

371
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:20,167
But the truth is,
you're nothing.

372
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:22,667
Hey, man, Calix.

373
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:24,333
- She's got guts.
- You're pretty bold.

374
00:26:24,467 --> 00:26:28,200
Yo, Miss Transferee,
for your information,

375
00:26:28,333 --> 00:26:30,300
Calix is the smartest student

376
00:26:30,433 --> 00:26:33,033
here at Brighton Bay Academy,
okay?

377
00:26:33,167 --> 00:26:35,900
No one can beat him
academically, okay?

378
00:26:36,033 --> 00:26:37,333
Know your place.

379
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:39,800
- As if.
- [TENSE MUSIC]

380
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:44,000
I just wanted to busk here.

381
00:26:44,267 --> 00:26:45,867
I was just hoping, Jacob.

382
00:26:46,133 --> 00:26:47,833
That Angel might be here
at Manila Park

383
00:26:47,967 --> 00:26:49,700
since this is where you met
before?

384
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:52,200
[ENGINE REVS]

385
00:26:52,333 --> 00:26:53,400
You've got a lot of energy.

386
00:26:53,533 --> 00:26:55,333
Why don't you go back
to the studio,

387
00:26:55,467 --> 00:26:57,067
meet up with your bandmates,

388
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,133
and finish your album?

389
00:26:59,500 --> 00:27:00,900
Wait, who's that?

390
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:03,200
We're not even open yet.

391
00:27:03,333 --> 00:27:05,233
[TENSE MUSIC]

392
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,633
Out of all the people
you could go up against

393
00:27:08,767 --> 00:27:10,933
here at Brighton Bay Academy,

394
00:27:11,067 --> 00:27:11,967
you chose me?

395
00:27:13,033 --> 00:27:15,067
I'm not afraid of you, Calix.

396
00:27:16,567 --> 00:27:18,567
Do it, Calix. Punch her.

397
00:27:18,700 --> 00:27:20,267
- Yeah, she deserves it.
- Come on.

398
00:27:22,533 --> 00:27:23,567
- Miguel.
- [CHUCKLES]

399
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:24,800
You seem distracted.

400
00:27:24,933 --> 00:27:26,733
Fix yourself. Smile, engage.

401
00:27:26,867 --> 00:27:28,800
They might think
you're being aloof.

402
00:27:28,933 --> 00:27:31,667
- Hm?
- Yes, Dad. Sorry.

403
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:33,533
- [SQUEALING]
- Siklab! Siklab!

404
00:27:33,667 --> 00:27:36,667
Siklab! Siklab! Siklab! Siklab!

405
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:40,500
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

406
00:27:40,633 --> 00:27:41,933
- [CLAPPING]
- We were amazing.

407
00:27:44,467 --> 00:27:46,267
Come on, smile.
We're in the lead.

408
00:27:49,667 --> 00:27:52,400
If it's okay with you,
I can lift you up.

409
00:27:52,533 --> 00:27:54,233
You seem familiar.

410
00:27:54,367 --> 00:27:58,567
<i> 'Cause baby, you are</i>

411
00:27:58,700 --> 00:28:00,967
<i>- My favorite song
- Yup. It's me, Angel.</i>

412
00:28:01,100 --> 00:28:01,700
[CHUCKLES]

413
00:28:01,833 --> 00:28:05,233
<i> You're my first hello to love</i>

414
00:28:05,367 --> 00:28:07,367
<i> My first, right where...</i>
